t-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/004059d03ed6794b58c59892411dae04/tumblr_odg3ydN3pT1rxzv9qo1_540.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 09-13-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:23:23-07:00","id":968597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/968493-1001-gadgets#post968493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really love the Idea's of Gadgets and thought it would fun for everyone to put up their best gadgets.<br /> <br /> 1.) A simple looking folding combat knife with Angelic Script written on it. The blade itself has an infinitely sharp edge<br /> <b>Activation and Trigger: </b>The Gadget is activated upon unfolding the blade.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When unfolding the blade it ignores all armor or stricture rating of anything the cutting edge come in contact with. equal to the users size rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Embed or Exploit is being used? I'd assume Walls of Jericho, based on the &quot;ignores all armor&quot; bit, but I don't know where you were intending to come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:55:50-07:00","id":968657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/968493-1001-gadgets?p=968597#post968597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Embed or Exploit is being used? I'd assume Walls of Jericho, based on the &quot;ignores all armor&quot; bit, but I don't know where you were intending to come from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah your right let me fix that<br /> <br /> I was using shatter being it destroy's objects. So I was thinking what if it only destroyed what is cutting not the whole object but what its cutting. So you could slice right through stuff. It only Ignores armor and Stricture rating so it would not help vs a vampires resilience","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 09-13-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:43:33-07:00","id":968714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/968493-1001-gadgets?p=968657#post968657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah your right let me fix that<br /> <br /> I was using shatter being it destroy's objects. So I was thinking what if it only destroyed what is cutting not the whole object but what its cutting. So you could slice right through stuff. It only Ignores armor and Stricture rating so it would not help vs a vampires resilience</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Okay. <hr /><br /> Might as well dump my list of gadgets from my notes:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><b>Gadgets</b></u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Embedded</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Murder Pistol</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Merciless Gunman): A semi-automatic pistol capable of killing entire groups of foes in moments, or doing grievous damage to priority targets. [Might need to downgrade due to embedded gadget limitations]</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hat of Blending</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Lost In The Crowd): As long as the wearer stays in large groups, they are nearly impossible to detect. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Bottomless Bandolier</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (In My Pocket): The armored pockets of this bandolier can produce a seeming endless number of grenades on demand.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Detective\u2019s Glasses</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Last Place You Look): These common sunglasses can reveal the presence things hidden with guilty intent.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Watchman\u2019s Alarm</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Last Place You Look) [Near-Field]: This small pocket sensor vibrates when someone who is trying to remain hidden is nearby.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Personal Soundtrack</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Like The Movies): When this cassette is played, the user can bend reality to conform to common media tropes.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Getaway Paintjob</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Quick Change): The driver of the vehicle bearing this paintjob can quickly switch between different appearance presets when unobserved, aiding in shaking pursuers.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Wolf\u2019s Bane Rounds</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Wave Function Collapse) [One Shot]: These silvered rifle rounds are capable of locking creatures in human form, preventing them from accessing their more destructive abilities.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Other variants might force creatures in other forms to assume their human one.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Trustworthy Suit</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (You Can Tell Me): The wearer of this impeccable 3-piece suit projects an air calm and trustworthiness. People around them feel like they can tell them anything over a drink or smoke.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Coat of Deflection</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Check Backdrop): Bullets seem to avoid the wearer of this long coat, unless enemies take the time to aim at them directly. The coat does get in the way of the wearer\u2019s own hasty shots, however.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Instruction Manuals</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Download Knowledge) [One Shot]: After a few minutes perusal of this book, the reader feels knowledgeable and confident about the upcoming task.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Distracting Magazine</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Ellipses): Whether it is the thought provoking articles, the gaudy advertisements, or the\u2026 \u201cvivid\u201d pictures, those who pick up and read this find time slipping away.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>McGuyver Kit</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Functional Identity): This toolbox/toolkit is able to convert nearly any other device into an impromptu weapon.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Performer\u2019s Blade</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Fungible Knowledge): This expertly crafted sword, disguised as a stage prop, is able to grant the wielder combat skill (Weaponry) commensurate to their acting ability (Expression).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Infiltration Map</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Like I Built It): This odd diagram reveals all the details and blueprints of whatever structure it is unrolled inside.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Joy Pills</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Miles Away) [One Shot, Near Field?]: This small smiley faced pills give a pleasant feeling that drives away other distracting emotions.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Danger Buzzer</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Read Hostility): This small earbud send out a sharp buzzing sound whenever the person the wearer is looking at is preparing to attack.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sacrificial Dolls</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Shift Consequences) [One Shot]: These small stuff dolls are capable of absorbing the damage from a single attack directed at their wearer, provided they are \u201cactivated\u201d beforehand.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Armor Vest</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Turn Blade): This kevlar vest reduces all incoming damage to mere pressure and bruises (Bashing).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Combat Dazzler</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Wasted Time): This LED sparkler makes it hard for foes to aim at the bearer, taking twice as long to draw a bead upon their target.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Avarice Grenades</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Apple of Discord) [One Shot]: These elaborate gold-plated grenades cause those who see them to (suicidally) want to keep them close, even fighting others to do so. They can be primed and ensure potential targets cluster around the blast area, or just thrown as a distraction or to flush foes from cover.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Match-Light</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Combustion): The target of this infrared laser becomes especially prone to spontaneous combustions, sometimes even catching fire outright.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Truce Flag</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Cool Heads Prevail): This simple white cloth, when waived, can cause hostility to cease between combatants.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Crash Padding</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Just Bruised): This set of padded clothing greatly protects its wearer from harm, reducing falls to a mere hard bump, and slashes to a small cut.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Night-Night Sap</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Knockout Punch): Most anyone hit with this leather sap finds themselves taking an impromptu vacation in unconsciousness.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Healing Poultice</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (On The Mend): This foul-smelling bandage can completely restore a person from a bruised wreck to full health in a fraction of an hour.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hack Drive</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Password Entropy): Plugging in this unassuming USB device can greatly assist in breaching password secured systems.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>\u201cSuicide\u201d Pills</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Play Possum) [One Shot]: This looks like an oral cyanide capsule, but when use merely fake death. Care should be taken to make sure others don\u2019t dispose of the \u201cbody\u201d in an\u2026 irreversible manner.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Echo Rifle</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Ripple): Damage inflicted with this rifle is always worse than it first seems, causing lingering wounds, or knocking the target into other hazards.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Door Busters</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Shatter) [One Shot]: This small explosive can breach even the toughest doors, when properly placed.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Bleeder Scope</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Victory At Any Price): When activated, this night-vision scope can guarantee a hit (1 automatic success on the next Firearms roll)\u2026 at some cost to the marksman.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Whisper Mike</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Across a Crowded Room): This small collar microphone can transmit a spoken message in a straight line to a target with perfect clarity.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Basilisk Trap</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (The Look): When this trap is triggered, a hypnotic scene plays that the triggerer can\u2019t look away from.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Auto-Pilot</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Alibi): This Palm Pilot PDA can be given to the Demon\u2019s detached Cover, and maintain it while to Demon carries out other actions. It can also be setup to activate in response to stimuli (such as someone knocking on the door).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Magic 8-ball</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Voice of the Machine): Shaking this normal looking novelty 8-ball and speaking a question aloud will have a relevant response appear.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exploited</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hellfire Muzzle</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Hellfire): A modular attachment to any gun that lets it fire blasts of incinerating flame.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Ring of Power</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Show of Power): This clearly unnatural ring is able to replicate the supernatural powers of a Mage upon call.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Demonic Transmission</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Demon Car): This mechanical contraption fuses with a vehicle, adding a number of modifications to its structure.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Vengeance Collar</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Eye For An Eye): When the wearer of this choker is subjected to an attack, the damage is removed and flung back at the attacker.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Instant Barrier</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Frozen In Time): The particles in this aerosol can can be sprayed and triggered to form a stationary and immovable cloud, blocking access points, forming cover, or turning high-speed objects into chunky salsa as they pass through the cloud.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Installation Tattoo Needle</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Living Installation): This weird tattoo needle allows a demon to install embeds upon humans.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Death Note</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Murder By Improbability): Writing someone\u2019s name in this eerie notebook will often end up with their \u201caccidental\u201d death.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Guardian Gargoyle</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Animate): This grotesque statuary can animate to attack intruders.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Introductory Video</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Context Matters): This short documentary explains the nature and capabilities of a single or small group of Unchained to 5 mortals, allowing them to assist in resisting cover violations. These are often part of the entry training for mortals joining an Agency.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Distortion Ward</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Fractured Space*): This Escheresque glyph subtly bends the space around the wearer, actually adding 20 range(?) between what appears to be the surface and then space nearby. This renders the wearer virtually immune to melee attacks, and can even affect ranged accuracy, but also means the wearer cannot physically interact with most objects. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Life Insurance</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Raise Dead) [One Shot]: This arcanely worded life insurance document can save a favored person\u2019s life - mostly by restoring it in the event it has been lost. On the event of the bearer\u2019s death, starting at 4 hours later, the owner begins rolling as per Raise Dead (minus adding Primum to the roll), up to a maximum of 5 days (after which, the gadget runs out of Aether to fuel the process). If successful, they are restored to life and the document crumbles to ash (if they aren\u2019t successful, they stay dead and the document still crumbles to ash).</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">* = Homebrewed Embed/Exploit, usually.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'll do some more formatting on these later.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:51:50-07:00","id":968973,"title":"","content":"Hot damn, those are cool. Might as well dump my concepts. <br /> <br /> Voice of Potence (Show of Power): A tape recorder that can record any supernatural power that works by sound and play it back, retaining any supernatural effects of the original ability. <br /> <br /> Eye of Potence (Show of Power): A more powerful version of the Voice of Potence. A video camera that can record supernatural powers and illusions and play them back. So, if it recorded a Nosferatu using Nightmare, the illusions created would be captured on film and would retain their power even when played back. <br /> <br /> Gary's Bones (Show of Power): A set of twenty-sided dice, capable of capturing one supernatural power or effect on each face. Once a die has been &quot;loaded&quot;, rolling it so that it lands on a &quot;loaded&quot; face causes the corresponding effect to occur. <br /> <br /> The Binding Rod (Ultimatum): Any contract or agreement signed with this pen is magically binding, and functions mechanically as a Changeling Pledge. <br /> <br /> Gourmand's Scalpel (Extispicy): A rather morbid Gadget in the shape of an ordinary kitchen knife. When it is used to cut a piece of flesh from a corpse, and the piece is consumed, the eater learns how and when the corpse perished, and certain other details: if they had a template, what template it was, and so on. <br /> <br /> The Fountain of Beelzebub (Addictive Presence): A plastic pumpkin-shaped Halloween candy bowl. Any candy left in it overnight becomes magically addictive, causing anyone who consumes it to become addicted to that type of candy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T02:33:36-07:00","id":969104,"title":"","content":"53) <br /> <b>Name:</b> Hidden Network<br /> <b>Embed Used:</b> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Special Message</span></span><br /> <b>Activation and Trigger:</b> The Gadget is activated upon making a phone call<br /> <b>Effect:</b> This software gadget is a hidden cellphone network. That hides it messages only for specific users. Upon making a phone call the users messages are hidden from everyone but the user the caller is calling. <br /> <br /> <u><b>This gadget is a car with multiple gadgets with in to create a spy car</b></u><br /> <br /> 54) <br /> <b>Name:</b> Transforming car <br /> <b>Embed Used: </b>Quick Change<br /> <b>Activation and Trigger:</b> Hidden button green in the steering wheel that need to be double tapped. <br /> <b>Effect:</b> This gadget allows a user to change aspects about their car. From the color, make and model or even just the plates. So the user can loose someone following them. <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Ram Plate <br /> <b>Embed Used: </b>Sabotage<br /> <b>Activation and Trigger:</b> Hidden button blue in the steering wheel that need to be double tapped.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Upon activating this gadget the users front bumper can cause enough damage to any car it hits to cause the car to ether shut down or wipe out.<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Deer in the headlights <br /> <b>Embed Used: </b>The Look<br /> <b>Activation and Trigger:</b> Hidden button red in the steering wheel that need to be double tapped.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Upon Activating this red high beam lights come on and causes anyone looking at the head lights to become frozen in place so the user can hit the person with their car. <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Where we're going we don't need roads<br /> <b>Demonic Form Used: </b>Wings<br /> <b>Activation and Trigger:</b> Hidden button white in the steering wheel that need to be double tapped.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Upon activating this gadget the wheels of the car fold flat to the road and begin to glow softly allowing the car to fly at the same speed it can move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T05:45:56-07:00","id":969163,"title":"","content":"Nice. I can see one using Lost In The Crowd for stealth during rush hour traffic. Or Data Form to &quot;summon&quot; the vehicle via cell phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","d